efy/lowdefy","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-18T20:19:18Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"11f1c0a8a5ddc10ccf8bdd86f73a50704bfb4c2f","github_link":"https://github.com/lowdefy/lowdefy/commit/11f1c0a8a5ddc10ccf8bdd86f73a50704bfb4c2f","commit_subject":"feat(blocks-native): Add the Menu block","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"lowdefy/lowdefy","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-18T20:19:18Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"c233454c9bbcf8ded3676da3a32a9015f0336760","github_link":"https://github.com/lowdefy/lowdefy/commit/c233454c9bbcf8ded3676da3a32a9015f0336760","commit_subject":"feat(blocks-native): Add the Sheet block","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"TeamHypersomnia/Hypersomnia","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-18T20:19:17Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"b2234181c5ecc3dda398c425dd0894567409c776","github_link":"https://github.com/TeamHypersomnia/Hypersomnia/commit/b2234181c5ecc3dda398c425dd0894567409c776","commit_subject":"Bots on a navmesh finer than the standard 128 collide with obstacles through their silhouette scaled down by cell size / 128 (0.5 at 64, 0.25 at 32): a massless copy colliding only with walls, glass and car floors, so they fit wherever the navmesh lets them walk. The real silhouette goes through obstacles but still takes every hit and collides with other characters - also when dead, so a corpse is never pushed through a thin wall. Items in a bot's hands go through obstacles too; a wall-only sensor copy knocks them against walls with the item's collision sound, at most once per 1.5 s per bot, louder the faster the bot moves (when_bot_item_knocked in sentience). Maps with the standard navmesh behave exactly as before. A 44 px corridor between two rooms on a cell-32 map: bots never entered it before, now they cross it; de_cyberaqua with cells 64 and 32: 0 desyncs, 100-200 knocks in 4 minutes; de_cyberaqua at 128: no extra fixtures, no knocks.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"GMOD/jbrowse-components","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-18T20:19:07Z","branch":"main","commit_sha